---
components: ["FunnelChart"]
description: Funnel chart draws the stages of a process as one tapered silhouette, with each stage's value and conversion beside it.
---

<script>
  import { FunnelChart } from "carbon-components-svelte/viz";

  const stages = [
    { id: "visit", label: "Visitors", value: 10000 },
    { id: "signup", label: "Signup", value: 6000 },
    { id: "activate", label: "Activated", value: 3000 },
    { id: "paid", label: "Paid", value: 900 },
  ];

  let selectedId;
</script>

`FunnelChart` is part of the data visualization subpackage. Import it from `carbon-components-svelte/viz` and load `carbon-components-svelte/css/viz.css` alongside `all.css`. With a single-theme stylesheet such as `g100.css`, load the matching `viz-g100.css` instead. The subpackage is experimental: its API may change in a minor release.

It is [FunnelBars](/components/FunnelBars) with a visible title, a tapered shape, and larger rows, and it takes the same props and events. Use `FunnelBars` directly for custom cells through its slots, or for a dense list where the silhouette does not matter.

## Basic

Pass `stages` and a `title`. Each stage keeps its honest width for most of its height, then slopes to meet the next one, so the stages read as one funnel without distorting the numbers.

<FunnelChart {stages} title="Signup funnel" />

## Rates

`rate` defaults to `"overall"`, the conversion from the first stage. Set it to `"step"`, `"both"`, or `"none"`.

<FunnelChart {stages} title="Signup funnel" rate="both" />

## Highlight

Set `highlight` to `"largest-drop"`, or to a stage id, to flag a stage with an icon and a color.

<FunnelChart {stages} title="Signup funnel" rate="step" highlight="largest-drop" />

## Shape

Set `shape` to `"bars"` for centered bars with no slopes between them.

<FunnelChart {stages} title="Signup funnel" shape="bars" />

## Color and size

<FunnelChart {stages} title="Signup funnel" color={3} size="md" />

## Selectable

Set `selectable` to put a toggle button in each row. Bind `selectedId` or listen for `select`.

<FunnelChart {stages} title="Pick a stage" selectable bind:selectedId />

## Accessibility

The funnel is a table: its caption is the title followed by the overall conversion, each stage is a row header, and the visually hidden column headers name the value and the rates. The shapes are hidden from assistive technology because the cells carry the same numbers. The visible title is hidden from it too, since the caption already says it. When `selectable`, the row buttons share one tab stop and the arrow keys move between them.
